<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή, δέ</span>) neg.
		Particle (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ</span>): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b> as Conj., <i>and not</i> (
				Ep.
			 also, <i>but not), nor</i>, connecting two whole
			clauses, used with the same constructions as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή, μή τι σὺ ταῦτα . . διείρεο μηδὲ
					μετάλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.550
				</span></i>
			, etc.: without a neg. preceding, <i><span class="en">
				4.302
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκνοῦσθαι, μηδ᾽ ἄπαιδα θνῄσκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					754
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				714
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				409
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδατος, μελίσσης, μηδὲ προσφέρειν μέθυ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					481
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.77
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ . . μηδέ</span> . . the first <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ.</span> may belong to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ</span> A, e.g. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.303
			</span></i> sq., or to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ</span> B, e.g.
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				391c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτε . . μηδέ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					2.45
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				327d
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτε</span> cannot follow
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ</span>:—for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ</span> after <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				11.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>B.</b> as
			Adv., joined with a single word or phrase, <i>not even,
				not either</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.375
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.710
			</span></i>, etc.; repeated emphatically, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδ᾽
				ὅντινα γαστέρι μήτηρ κοῦρον ἐόντα φέροι μηδ᾽ ὃς
			φύγοι</span> let <i>not</i> the babe unborn —<i>no
				let not even</i> it escape, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.58
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μήποτ᾽ αὖθις μηδ᾽ ἀναστῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					569
				</span></i>
			:—for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ τι</span>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήτις</span>
			.</div>
